<h3>How the three levers are picked</h3>
<p>After the tenth answer, the startup scorecard divides your points in each area by that area's maximum and sorts the areas from weakest to strongest. The three weakest become your levers, each with one concrete next step. Because it uses the share of the maximum rather than raw points, a weak answer on runway (worth 6) can rank as a lever just as a weak answer on growth (worth 14) can.</p>
